  "narrative": [
    {
      "text": "SOERGEL CALCULUS — The monoidal category of Soergel bimodules is an incarnation of the Hecke category, a fundamental object in representation theory.\n\n**SOERGEL CALCULUS**\n\n*BEN ELIAS AND GEORDIE WILLIAMSON*\n\n83 pp, 46 sections.\n\n**Abstract.** The monoidal category of Soergel bimodules is an incarnation of the Hecke category, a fundamental object in representation theory. We present this cat- egory by generators and relations, using the language of planar diagrammatics. We show that Libedinsky’s light leaves give a basis for morphism spaces and give a new proof of Soergel’s classiﬁcation of the indecomposable Soergel bimodules.\n\n**Outline.** Front matter; 1 Introduction; 1.1 The Hecke algebra by generators and relati; 1.2 The Hecke category; 1.3 Soergel bimodules; 1.4 Soergel bimodules by generators and relati; 1.4.1 One color relations:; 1.4.2 Two color relations:; 1.4.3 Three color or ``Zamolodchikov'' relatio; 1.5 Consequences for the structure of Soergel ; 1.6 Organization of the paper; 2 The Hecke Algebra; 1.7 Acknowledgements; 2.1 Basic definitions; 2.2 The Kazhdan-Lusztig basis; 2.3 The presentation in the Kazhdan-Lusztig ge; 2.4 The standard trace and the defect formula; 3 Soergel Bimodules",
